\fBOrigin\fR
Bareos console command.
.SS "cancel"
Cancel a job
.PP
\fBSynopsis\fR
.nf
cancel [storage=<storage>] [sd=<sd>] [jobid=<jobid>[,...]] [job=<job>] [ujobid=<ujobid>] [state=<state>] [all] [yes]
.fi
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Cancels running or waiting jobs; without a selection the Director asks for one.
.PP
\fBArguments\fR
.PP
\fIcancel\fR
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Jobs of a storage (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "sd=<sd>"
Storage name (as storage=) (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "jobid=<jobid>[,...]"
Job ID (text; several values separated by commas)
.TP
.B "job=<job>"
Job name (name; values from .jobs)
.TP
.B "ujobid=<ujobid>"
Unique job name (text)
.TP
.B "state=<state>"
Jobs in this state (created, blocked, waiting, running) (text)
.TP
.B "all"
Every job (keyword)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.TP
.B "cancel jobid=42"
cancel job 42 after confirmation
.TP
.B "cancel job=BackupClient1 yes"
cancel the running BackupClient1 job without asking
.TP
.B "cancel state=waiting yes"
cancel every waiting job
.PP
\fBOrigin\fR
Bareos console command.
.SS "restore"
Restore files
.PP
\fBSynopsis\fR
.nf
restore [where=<where>] [client=<client>] [storage=<storage>] [bootstrap=<bootstrap>] [restorejob=<restorejob>] [comment=<comment>] [jobid=<jobid>[,...]] [fileset=<fileset>] [replace=<always|ifnewer|ifolder|never>] [pluginoptions=<pluginoptions>] [regexwhere=<regexwhere>] [fileregex=<fileregex>] [ovfs=<ovfs>] [restoreclient=<restoreclient>] [backupformat=<backupformat>] [pool=<pool>] [file=<file> ...] [directory=<directory> ...] [before[=<before>]] [strip_prefix=<strip_prefix>] [stripprefix=<stripprefix>] [add_prefix=<add_prefix>] [addprefix=<addprefix>] [add_suffix=<add_suffix>] [addsuffix=<addsuffix>] [select[=<select>]] [current] [copies] [archive] [done] [all] [job=<job>] [yes] [catalog=<catalog>]
.fi
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Selects files from backups and starts a restore job. Without a selection the Director shows the selection menu; `done` ends the file selection.
.PP
\fBArguments\fR
.PP
\fIrestore\fR
.TP
.B "where=<where>"
Restore prefix (text)
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
Client name (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Storage name (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "bootstrap=<bootstrap>"
Bootstrap file (text)
.TP
.B "restorejob=<restorejob>"
Restore job (name; values from .jobs)
.TP
.B "comment=<comment>"
Comment (text)
.TP
.B "jobid=<jobid>[,...]"
Job IDs (text; several values separated by commas)
.TP
.B "fileset=<fileset>"
FileSet name (name; values from .filesets)
.TP
.B "replace=<always|ifnewer|ifolder|never>"
Replace mode (one of a fixed set; values: always, ifnewer, ifolder, never)
.TP
.B "pluginoptions=<pluginoptions>"
Plugin options (text)
.TP
.B "regexwhere=<regexwhere>"
Restore path rewrite (text)
.TP
.B "fileregex=<fileregex>"
Select files by regex (text)
.TP
.B "ovfs=<ovfs>"
Restore IDs of OVFS nodes (Onesimus): JobId:FileIndex,... (text)
.TP
.B "restoreclient=<restoreclient>"
Restore client (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "backupformat=<backupformat>"
Backup format (text)
.TP
.B "pool=<pool>"
Pool name (name; values from .pools)
.TP
.B "file=<file> ..."
File to restore (text; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "directory=<directory> ..."
Directory to restore (text; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "before[=<before>]"
Most recent backup before this time (text; the value may be left out)
.TP
.B "strip_prefix=<strip_prefix>"
Strip prefix (text)
.TP
.B "stripprefix=<stripprefix>"
Strip prefix (text)
.TP
.B "add_prefix=<add_prefix>"
Add prefix (text)
.TP
.B "addprefix=<addprefix>"
Add prefix (text)
.TP
.B "add_suffix=<add_suffix>"
Add suffix (text)
.TP
.B "addsuffix=<addsuffix>"
Add suffix (text)
.TP
.B "select[=<select>]"
Select (text; the value may be left out)
.TP
.B "current"
Most recent backup (keyword)
.TP
.B "copies"
Use copies (keyword)
.TP
.B "archive"
Use archive jobs (keyword)
.TP
.B "done"
End the selection (keyword)
.TP
.B "all"
Select every file (keyword)
.TP
.B "job=<job>"
Job name (name; values from .jobs)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.TP
.B "catalog=<catalog>"
Catalog name (name; values from .catalogs)
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.TP
.B "restore client=fd select current all done yes where=/tmp/r"
restore everything of a client
.TP
.B "restore"
open the selection menu
.TP
.B "restore jobid=42 client=bareos\-fd restorejob=RestoreFiles where=/tmp/bareos\-restores all done yes"
restore all files of job 42 to a separate directory
.TP
.B "restore client=bareos\-fd restorejob=RestoreFiles file=/etc/fstab where=/tmp/bareos\-restores yes"
restore a single file from the latest backup
.PP
\fBOrigin\fR
Bareos console command.
.SS "enable"
Enable a job/client/schedule
.PP
\fBSynopsis\fR
.nf
enable [job=<job>] [client=<client>] [schedule=<schedule>] [storage=<storage>]
.fi
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Switches a job, client or schedule back on that was switched off with disable. An enabled job is started by its schedule again, an enabled client is backed up again. Without an argument, or with job, client or schedule without a value, the Director offers the disabled resources of that kind; if there is exactly one it is selected automatically.
.PP
The change lives only in the memory of the running Director and is lost at the next reload or restart. A permanent setting requires the Enabled directive in the configuration. The catalog is not changed.
.PP
\fBArguments\fR
.PP
\fIenable\fR
.TP
.B "job=<job>"
Job name (name; values from .jobs)
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
Client name (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "schedule=<schedule>"
Schedule name (name; values from .schedule)
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Storage name (name; values from .storages)
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.TP
.B "enable job=BackupClient1"
let the scheduler start BackupClient1 again
.TP
.B "enable client=bareos\-fd"
back up the client bareos\-fd again
.TP
.B "enable schedule=WeeklyCycle"
reactivate a schedule
.PP
\fBOrigin\fR
Bareos console command.
.SS "disable"
Disable a job/client/schedule
.PP
\fBSynopsis\fR
.nf
disable [job=<job>] [client=<client>] [schedule=<schedule>] [storage=<storage>]
.fi
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Switches a job, client or schedule off. A disabled job is no longer started by its schedule, a disabled client is no longer backed up, a disabled schedule triggers no jobs. A disabled job can still be started by hand with run. Without an argument, or with job, client or schedule without a value, the Director offers the enabled resources of that kind.
.PP
The change lives only in the memory of the running Director until the next reload or restart. A permanent setting requires Enabled = no in the configuration.
.PP
\fBArguments\fR
.PP
\fIdisable\fR
.TP
.B "job=<job>"
Job name (name; values from .jobs)
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
Client name (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "schedule=<schedule>"
Schedule name (name; values from .schedule)
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Storage name (name; values from .storages)
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.TP
.B "disable job=BackupClient1"
stop scheduled runs of BackupClient1 until the next reload
.TP
.B "disable client=bareos\-fd"
skip the client during maintenance
.TP
.B "disable schedule=WeeklyCycle"
suspend a schedule
.PP
\fBOrigin\fR
Bareos console command.
.SS "list"
List objects from catalog
.PP
\fBSynopsis\fR
.nf
list [limit=<limit>] [offset=<offset>] [current] [enabled | disabled] [catalog=<catalog>]
list basefiles [jobid=<jobid>] [ujobid=<ujobid>]
list backups client=<client> [fileset=<fileset>] [jobstatus=<jobstatus>] [level=<F|I|D>[,...]] [order=<asc|desc|ascending|descending>] [days=<days>] [hours=<hours>] [reverse]
list client=<client>
list clients
list copies [jobid=<jobid>[,...]]
list files [jobid=<jobid>] [ujobid=<ujobid>] [type=<type>]
list filesets
list fileset[=<fileset>] [filesetid=<filesetid>] [jobid=<jobid>] [ujobid=<ujobid>]
list jobs [client=<client>] [jobstatus=<jobstatus>[,...]] [jobtype=<jobtype>[,...]] [joblevel=<joblevel>[,...]] [level=<level>[,...]] [volume=<volume>] [pool=<pool>] [days=<days>] [hours=<hours>] [last] [count] [reverse] [job=<job>] [jobname=<jobname>] [jobid=<jobid>[,...]] [ujobid=<ujobid>] [fileset=<fileset>]
list job=<job> [client=<client>] [jobstatus=<jobstatus>[,...]] [jobtype=<jobtype>[,...]] [joblevel=<joblevel>[,...]] [level=<level>[,...]] [volume=<volume>] [pool=<pool>] [days=<days>] [hours=<hours>] [last] [count] [reverse] [jobname=<jobname>] [jobid=<jobid>[,...]] [ujobid=<ujobid>] [fileset=<fileset>]
list jobname=<jobname> [client=<client>] [jobstatus=<jobstatus>[,...]] [jobtype=<jobtype>[,...]] [joblevel=<joblevel>[,...]] [level=<level>[,...]] [volume=<volume>] [pool=<pool>] [days=<days>] [hours=<hours>] [last] [count] [reverse] [jobname=<jobname>] [jobid=<jobid>[,...]] [ujobid=<ujobid>] [fileset=<fileset>]
list jobid=<jobid>[,...]
list ujobid=<ujobid>
list joblog [jobid=<jobid>] [ujobid=<ujobid>] [count] [reverse]
list jobmedia [jobid=<jobid>] [ujobid=<ujobid>]
list jobtotals
list jobstatistics [jobid=<jobid>] [job=<job>]
list log [client=<client>] [reverse]
list media[=<media>] [jobid=<jobid>] [ujobid=<ujobid>] [pool=<pool>] [all]
list nextvolume [job=<job>] [days=<days>]
list pools
list pool=<pool>
list poolid=<poolid>
list storages
list storage=<storage>
list volumes [jobid=<jobid>] [ujobid=<ujobid>] [pool=<pool>] [all] [count]
list volume=<volume>
list volumeid=<volumeid>
list mediaid=<mediaid>
list schedules
.fi
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Lists catalog records; llist prints every field of each record. `limit=` and `offset=` page through the result, `current` limits to records of configured resources, `enabled`/`disabled` to resources in that state.
.PP
\fBSubcommands\fR
.TP
.B "list basefiles"
Base files of a job
.IP
Lists the base files of a job that used a Base job, that is the files taken over from the base backup instead of being saved again; jobid= or ujobid= is required.
.TP
.B "list backups"
Backups of a client
.IP
Lists the backups of one client; client= is required. fileset= limits the listing to one FileSet, fileset=any includes all of them. jobstatus=, level=, days= and hours= filter as with list jobs, order=asc or order=desc sorts by start time; any other order value is an error.
.IP
Without client= the reply is "missing parameter: client". A FileSet outside the FileSet ACL of the console gives "Access to specified FileSet not allowed."
.TP
.B "list client=<client>"
One client
.IP
Shows the catalog record of one client by name. list client without a value is not a valid keyword and gives "Unknown list keyword".
.TP
.B "list clients"
Every client
.IP
Lists every client record of the catalog with id, name, file retention and job retention; llist adds the uname and autoprune setting. enabled or disabled keep only clients in that state in the configuration, current only clients still configured.
.TP
.B "list copies"
Copies of jobs
.IP
Lists copy jobs together with the job they were copied from and the media type. jobid= takes one JobId or a comma\-separated list and limits the listing to copies of or made by these jobs. If there are no copy jobs, the reply is empty.
.TP
.B "list files"
Files of a job
.IP
Lists the paths of all files saved by one job, including the base files it refers to; jobid= or ujobid= is required. limit= and offset= do not shorten the text listing, they only appear in the range information of API mode 2.
.TP
.B "list filesets"
Every FileSet
.IP
Lists every FileSet record of the catalog with id, name, MD5 sum, creation time and FileSet text. A FileSet gets a new record whenever its definition changes; current keeps only FileSets still defined in the configuration.
.TP
.B "list fileset[=<fileset>]"
One FileSet
.IP
Shows one FileSet record of the catalog, including the stored FileSet text and its MD5 sum. The record is selected by filesetid= or by the job that used it with jobid= or ujobid=; without one of them the command reports an error.
.TP
.B "list jobs"
Jobs
.IP
Lists the jobs of the catalog, one row per job. The filters can be combined: job= or jobname=, client=, jobstatus= (letters such as T, E, f or names such as error, comma\-separated), jobtype= (letter or exact name such as Backup), joblevel= or level= (F, I, D or Full, Incremental, Differential), volume=, pool=, days= and hours=. last keeps only the latest run per job name, count prints just the number of rows, reverse shows the newest first.
.IP
limit= and offset= page through the result. For a console with ACLs the limit is applied before the rows the console may not see are removed, so a limited listing can come out shorter or even empty. An unknown jobtype or level is an error.
.TP
.B "list job=<job>"
Jobs of one name
.IP
Lists the jobs with the given job name; it works like list jobs job=<name> and accepts the same filters.
.TP
.B "list jobname=<jobname>"
Jobs of one name
.TP
.B "list jobid=<jobid>[,...]"
One job
.IP
Lists exactly the job with this JobId; llist jobid= shows all its fields one below the other. An unknown JobId gives an empty reply, and list jobid without a value reports "Missing jobid parameter".
.TP
.B "list ujobid=<ujobid>"
One job
.TP
.B "list joblog"
Log of a job
.IP
Prints the stored log of one job with time stamps; jobid= or ujobid= selects the job. count prints only the number of log lines. An unknown JobId or a job the console may not access gives "jobid not found in db, access to job or client denied by ACL, or client not found in db".
.TP
.B "list jobmedia"
Volumes of a job
.IP
Shows which volumes a job wrote, with the first and last file index on each volume; without jobid= or ujobid= the records of all jobs are listed. llist adds the media id, start and end file and block.
.TP
.B "list jobtotals"
Totals per job name
.IP
Shows the number of jobs, files and bytes per job name for backup, archive and copy jobs, followed by the totals over all of them. In API mode 2 the rows are under "jobs" and the sums under "jobtotals".
.TP
.B "list jobstatistics"
Statistics of a job
.IP
Lists the statistics samples (sample time, files and bytes) recorded for a running or finished job; jobid= is required. Without it, or for a job the console may not access, the reply is "no jobid given"; a job without statistics gives "No results to list." The alias jobstats is accepted.
.TP
.B "list log"
Director log
.IP
Prints the most recent log lines of all jobs from the catalog, by default the last five; limit= changes the number. client= restricts them to jobs of one client, an unknown client gives "invalid client argument". The lines appear oldest first, reverse puts the newest first.
.TP
.B "list media[=<media>]"
Volumes
.IP
Alias of list volumes: without a value it lists the volumes grouped by pool and takes the same keywords all, pool=, jobid= and ujobid=; with a value, media=<name>, it shows that single volume like list volume=.
.TP
.B "list nextvolume"
Next volume of a job
.IP
Shows which volume a job would write next, once for every scheduled run within the coming days; days= sets how many days to look ahead (at most 50, other values are ignored with a warning). Without job= the Director lists the job resources and asks for one; a dot aborts. For jobs that write no volume, such as restore jobs, it reports that no next volume can be found.
.IP
Deviation from Bareos: for an unknown job odir reports success, whereas Bareos returns an error. In API mode 2 the result is empty.
.TP
.B "list pools"
Every pool
.IP
Lists every pool record of the catalog with id, name, number of volumes, maximum volumes, pool type and label format. llist adds all other fields of the records.
.TP
.B "list pool=<pool>"
One pool
.IP
Shows the catalog record of one pool by name; poolid= selects it by id instead.
.TP
.B "list poolid=<poolid>"
One pool
.TP
.B "list storages"
Every storage
.IP
Lists every storage record of the catalog. current, enabled and disabled restrict the listing to storages still configured or in that state.
.TP
.B "list storage=<storage>"
One storage
.TP
.B "list volumes"
Volumes
.IP
Lists the volumes of the catalog grouped by pool. all prints them in one table, pool= restricts the listing to one pool, jobid= or ujobid= shows only the names of the volumes a job used, and count prints the number of volumes per pool. media is an alias with the same keywords.
.IP
If the pool given with pool= is not in the catalog, the Director lists the defined pools and asks for a selection; a dot aborts. In API mode 2 there is no question and the error is returned directly.
.TP
.B "list volume=<volume>"
One volume
.IP
Shows exactly one volume by its name, with status, bytes, retention, slot, media type and last write time. volumeid= and mediaid= select it by its media id instead.
.TP
.B "list volumeid=<volumeid>"
One volume
.TP
.B "list mediaid=<mediaid>"
One volume
.TP
.B "list schedules"
Not a catalog list: answered as unknown keyword (see show schedules)
.IP
Schedules are configuration resources and have no table in the catalog, so like Bareos odir answers "Unknown list keyword: schedules". Use show schedules for the schedule resources and show disabled schedules for the disabled ones.
.PP
