.SS "estimate"
Performs FileSet estimate, listing gives full listing
.PP
\fBSynopsis\fR
.nf
estimate [job=<job>] [client=<client>] [fd=<fd>] [fileset=<fileset>] [level=<level>] [accurate=<yes|no>] [listing] [catalog=<catalog>]
.fi
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Asks the File Daemon how many files and bytes a backup job would save at the chosen level, without starting a job. The Director connects to the client, sends fileset and level and prints the answer; with listing every file that would be saved is printed as well. Without job= the Director offers the list of jobs.
.PP
level=, client= (or fd=), fileset= and accurate= override the values of the job. Only native clients are supported, not NDMP. Nothing is changed; for Incremental and Differential the catalog is only read to find the last matching job.
.PP
\fBArguments\fR
.PP
\fIestimate\fR
.TP
.B "job=<job>"
Job name (name; values from .jobs)
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
Client name (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "fd=<fd>"
Client name (as client=) (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "fileset=<fileset>"
FileSet name (name; values from .filesets)
.TP
.B "level=<level>"
Backup level (one of a fixed set; values: Full, Incremental, Differential, VirtualFull, Base, Since, VolumeToCatalog, DiskToCatalog, Catalog, Data, InitCatalog)
.TP
.B "accurate=<yes|no>"
Accurate mode (yes or no)
.TP
.B "listing"
List every file (keyword)
.TP
.B "catalog=<catalog>"
Catalog name (name; values from .catalogs)
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.TP
.B "estimate job=BackupClient1 level=Full"
size of a full backup of BackupClient1
.TP
.B "estimate job=BackupClient1 level=Incremental listing"
every file the next incremental would save
.PP
