A volume record
.IP
Deletes a volume and every job stored on it from the catalog. The data on the medium is untouched, but it can no longer be selected for restore. Without a name the pool and volume are selected in a dialogue; pool= sets the pool for this selection. The Director asks for confirmation unless yes is given; the action cannot be undone.
.IP
Onesimus deviation: a volume holding jobs of the latest Full chain of a client and FileSet is never deleted, not even with yes.
.TP
.B "delete pool[=<pool>]"
A pool record
.IP
Deletes a Pool record from the catalog after confirmation; without a name the pool is chosen from a list. Onesimus deviation: deleting pools is not implemented yet, and after yes the Director answers delete pool: not supported.
.TP
.B "delete jobid=<jobid>[,...]"
Job records (list or ranges)
.IP
Deletes jobs together with their file and JobMedia records from the catalog. The value may be a comma\-separated list with ranges such as 507\-509,511; a range of more than 25 JobIds requires confirmation. Without a value the Director asks for the JobId. This is also the way to remove a single job of a protected latest Full chain.
.TP
.B "delete storage[=<storage>]"
A storage record
.IP
Deletes an orphaned Storage record from the catalog, one that no longer exists in the configuration. A storage still configured is refused; remove it from the configuration first. Without a value the Director asks for the name.
.PP
\fBArguments\fR
.PP
\fIdelete\fR
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.TP
.B "catalog=<catalog>"
Catalog name (name; values from .catalogs)
.PP
\fIdelete volume[=<volume>]\fR
.TP
.B "volume[=<volume>]"
Volume name (name; values from .media; the value may be left out)
.TP
.B "pool=<pool>"
Pool of the volumes to select (name; values from .pools)
.PP
\fIdelete pool[=<pool>]\fR
.TP
.B "pool[=<pool>]"
Pool name (name; values from .pools; the value may be left out)
.PP
\fIdelete jobid=<jobid>[,...]\fR
.TP
.B "jobid=<jobid>[,...]"
Job IDs (text; several values separated by commas)
.PP
\fIdelete storage[=<storage>]\fR
.TP
.B "storage[=<storage>]"
Storage name (name; values from .storages; the value may be left out)
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Storage name (name; values from .storages)
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.TP
.B "delete"
choose what to delete from the menu
.TP
.B "delete jobid=507\-509,511"
delete four job records
.TP
.B "delete volume=Full\-0001 yes"
delete a volume without asking
.TP
.B "delete volume pool=Scratch"
choose the volume to delete from pool Scratch
.TP
.B "delete pool=Scratch"
ask to delete the Scratch pool record
.TP
.B "delete jobid=14"
delete one job record
.TP
.B "delete jobid=600,602"
delete two job records
.TP
.B "delete storage=OldTape"
remove the catalog record of a removed storage
.PP
\fBOrigin\fR
Bareos console command.
.SS "prune"
Prune records from catalog
.PP
\fBSynopsis\fR
.nf
prune
prune files [client=<client>] [pool=<pool>] [yes]
prune jobs [client=<client>] [pool=<pool>] [jobtype=<jobtype>] [yes]
prune volume[=<volume>] [all] [pool=<pool>] [yes]
prune stats [yes]
prune directory[=<directory>] [client=<client>] [recursive] [yes]
.fi
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Removes expired catalog records, respecting the retention periods.
.PP
\fBSubcommands\fR
.TP
.B "prune files"
File records
.IP
Removes file records whose File Retention has expired, for one client (client=) or for the retention of a pool (pool=); without client= the client is chosen from a list. The Director shows the retention period and asks yes/mod/no, where mod sets a different period for the running Director until the next reload; yes skips the question. Full access to the involved resources is required.
.IP
Onesimus deviation: the file records of the latest Full chain of every client and FileSet are always kept.
.TP
.B "prune jobs"
Job records
.IP
Removes job records whose Job Retention has expired, for one client (client=), a pool (pool=) or a job type (jobtype=). The Director shows the retention period and asks yes/mod/no unless yes is given. Full access to the involved resources is required.
.IP
Onesimus deviation: the latest successful Full chain of every client and FileSet name is never pruned, even if it is older than the retention and even when job, FileSet or client are no longer configured. If that chain cannot be determined, nothing is deleted.
.TP
.B "prune volume[=<volume>]"
Volume records
.IP
Removes the jobs of a volume whose Volume Retention has expired; the volume must have status Full or Used. Without a name the pool and volume are selected in a dialogue. all prunes every volume, of one pool with pool=. The Director asks yes/mod/no unless yes is given.
.IP
Onesimus deviation: a volume holding jobs of the latest Full chain of a client and FileSet is never pruned.
.TP
.B "prune stats"
Job statistics
.IP
Removes entries from JobHisto, DeviceStats and JobStats that are older than the Statistics Retention. The Director shows the retention period and asks unless yes is given.
.TP
.B "prune directory[=<directory>]"
Directory cache
.IP
Removes the file records below one directory from the catalog; recursive includes subdirectories. Without client= the Director first asks whether the directory should be removed for all clients, and without a path it asks for the full path. yes skips the confirmation.
.PP
\fBArguments\fR
.PP
\fIprune files\fR
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
Client name (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "pool=<pool>"
Pool name (name; values from .pools)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.PP
\fIprune jobs\fR
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
Client name (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "pool=<pool>"
Pool name (name; values from .pools)
.TP
.B "jobtype=<jobtype>"
Job type (text)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.PP
\fIprune volume[=<volume>]\fR
.TP
.B "volume[=<volume>]"
Volume name (name; values from .media; the value may be left out)
.TP
.B "all"
Every volume (keyword)
.TP
.B "pool=<pool>"
Pool name (name; values from .pools)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.PP
\fIprune stats\fR
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.PP
\fIprune directory[=<directory>]\fR
.TP
.B "directory[=<directory>]"
Directory (text; the value may be left out)
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
Client name (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "recursive"
With subdirectories (keyword)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.TP
.B "prune"
choose what to prune from the menu
.TP
.B "prune jobs client=bareos\-fd yes"
remove expired job records of bareos\-fd
.TP
.B "prune files client=bareos\-fd yes"
prune expired file records of bareos\-fd
.TP
.B "prune jobs pool=Incremental yes"
prune expired jobs using the retention of pool Incremental
.TP
.B "prune volume=Full\-0001 yes"
prune one volume without asking
.TP
.B "prune volume all pool=Full"
prune every volume of pool Full after confirmation
.TP
.B "prune stats yes"
prune old statistics without asking
.TP
.B "prune directory=/var/cache client=bareos\-fd recursive yes"
drop /var/cache and below from the catalog of bareos\-fd
.PP
\fBOrigin\fR
Bareos console command.
.SS "purge"
Purge records from catalog
.PP
\fBSynopsis\fR
.nf
purge [catalog=<catalog>]
purge files [job=<job>] [jobid=<jobid>[,...]] [client=<client>] [volume=<volume>] [yes]
purge jobs [client=<client>] [volume=<volume>] [pool=<pool>] [jobstatus=<jobstatus>[,...]] [yes]
purge volume[=<volume>] [all] [pool=<pool> | allpools] [volstatus=<volstatus>[,...]] [volume=<volume> ...] [storage=<storage>] [devicetype=<devicetype>] [drive=<drive>] [action=<truncate|all>] [dryrun | yes]
purge quota [client=<client>] [yes]
.fi
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Deletes catalog records without regard to retention periods. It needs full access to every resource.
.PP
purge volume all (Onesimus extension) purges every volume of one pool (pool=) or of all pools the console may access (allpools) whose status is one of volstatus= (default Full,Used,Error). It is never interactive: dryrun only shows what would be purged, yes purges.
.PP
\fBSubcommands\fR
.TP
.B "purge files"
File records
.IP
Deletes file records from the catalog regardless of retention periods, for one job (job= or jobid=), a client or a volume; the jobs themselves stay. Like every purge it prints a warning, needs full access to all resources and cannot be undone.
.IP
Onesimus deviation: the file records of the latest Full chain of a client and FileSet are skipped, and each purge runs in one transaction whose errors are reported instead of ignored.
.TP
.B "purge jobs"
Job records
.IP
Deletes whole jobs with all their records regardless of retention periods, for a client, a volume or a pool. jobstatus= limits this to jobs with the given status letters (T, E, f, ...) or names such as error, separated by commas. The Director counts the jobs and asks Purge (yes/no)? unless yes is given. A volume left without jobs becomes Purged.
.IP
Onesimus deviation: jobs of the latest Full chain of a client and FileSet are skipped, and each purge runs in one transaction whose errors are reported.
.TP
.B "purge volume[=<volume>]"
Volume records
.IP
Deletes every job on a volume from the catalog regardless of retention; the volume then becomes Purged and can be reused. Several volume= may be given, and each is confirmed on its own unless yes is given. action=truncate or all runs the ActionOnPurge on Purged volumes through the Storage Daemon, with storage=, pool= or allpools, devicetype= and drive=. A volume holding the latest Full chain of a client is never purged (Onesimus).
.IP
Onesimus extension: purge volume all purges every volume of pool= or of all permitted pools (allpools) whose status is in volstatus=, by default Full, Used and Error. Purged and Recycle volumes are never selected and Cleaning tapes cannot be purged. It never asks: exactly one of dryrun (preview) and yes is required, and refused volumes are skipped with their reason.
.TP
.B "purge quota"
Quota of a client
.IP
Resets the quota counters of a client; without client= the client is chosen from a list. Like every purge it prints a warning and needs full access to all resources.
.PP
\fBArguments\fR
.PP
\fIpurge\fR
.TP
.B "catalog=<catalog>"
Catalog name (name; values from .catalogs)
.PP
\fIpurge files\fR
.TP
.B "job=<job>"
Job name (name; values from .jobs)
.TP
.B "jobid=<jobid>[,...]"
Job IDs (text; several values separated by commas)
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
Client name (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "volume=<volume>"
Volume name (name; values from .media)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.PP
\fIpurge jobs\fR
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
Client name (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "volume=<volume>"
Volume name (name; values from .media)
.TP
.B "pool=<pool>"
Pool name (name; values from .pools)
.TP
.B "jobstatus=<jobstatus>[,...]"
Job status letters (text; several values separated by commas)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.PP
\fIpurge volume[=<volume>]\fR
.TP
.B "volume[=<volume>]"
Volume name (name; values from .media; the value may be left out)
.TP
.B "all"
Every volume of the pool selection (Onesimus) (keyword)
.TP
.B "pool=<pool>"
Pool name (name; values from .pools; excludes the other arguments of group scope)
.TP
.B "allpools"
Every pool (keyword; excludes the other arguments of group scope)
.TP
.B "volstatus=<volstatus>[,...]"
Volume status (Onesimus); Purged and Recycle volumes are never selected, Cleaning tapes cannot be purged (one of a fixed set; values: Full, Used, Error, Append, Archive, Disabled, Read\-Only; several values separated by commas)
.TP
.B "volume=<volume> ..."
Volumes for action= (several allowed) (name; values from .media; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Storage name (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "devicetype=<devicetype>"
Device type (text)
.TP
.B "drive=<drive>"
Drive number (number)
.TP
.B "action=<truncate|all>"
Action on purge (one of a fixed set; values: truncate, all)
.TP
.B "dryrun"
Only show what would be purged (Onesimus) (keyword; excludes the other arguments of group mode)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword; excludes the other arguments of group mode)
.PP
\fIpurge quota\fR
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
Client name (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.TP
.B "purge volume=Full\-0001 yes"
purge one volume
.TP
.B "purge volume all pool=Full volstatus=Full,Used dryrun"
show what would be purged (Onesimus)
.TP
.B "purge volume all allpools yes"
purge every Full, Used or Error volume (Onesimus)
.TP
.B "purge"
choose what to purge from the menu
.TP
.B "purge jobs client=bareos\-fd jobstatus=E"
purge the failed jobs of bareos\-fd
.TP
.B "purge files jobid=599"
purge the file records of job 599
.TP
.B "purge files client=bareos\-fd yes"
purge all file records of bareos\-fd
.TP
.B "purge jobs volume=Full\-0001 yes"
purge every job on volume Full\-0001
.TP
.B "purge jobs pool=Incremental jobstatus=E,f"
purge the failed jobs of pool Incremental
.TP
.B "purge volume action=truncate storage=File pool=Full"
truncate the purged volumes of pool Full
.TP
.B "purge volume all pool=Incremental volstatus=Error dryrun"
preview purging the Error volumes of Incremental (Onesimus)
.TP
.B "purge quota client=bareos\-fd"
reset the quota of bareos\-fd
.PP
\fBOrigin\fR
Bareos console command.
.SS "truncate"
Truncate purged volumes
.PP
\fBSynopsis\fR
.nf
truncate volstatus=<Purged> [storage=<storage>] [pool=<pool>] [volume=<volume>[,...]] [drive=<drive>] [yes] [catalog=<catalog>]
.fi
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Frees the space of volumes whose jobs have already been removed (status Purged). The Director lists the matching volumes, asks for confirmation and has the Storage Daemon relabel them, which shrinks the volume file or tape to its label. The volumes stay in the catalog. Only native (non\-NDMP) storages are supported, and only the volumes of one storage per call.
.PP
volstatus=Purged is required. storage=, pool= and volume= narrow the selection; an unknown storage or pool opens a selection list. drive= selects the drive, yes skips the question. Other keywords, including client= and catalog=, end with Invalid parameter. Under API 1 and 2 nothing is asked, so without yes nothing happens.
.PP
Onesimus deviation: a volume holding jobs of the latest Full chain of a client and FileSet is never truncated.
.PP
\fBArguments\fR
.PP
\fItruncate\fR
.TP
.B "volstatus=<Purged>"
Only Purged volumes (one of a fixed set; values: Purged; required)
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Storage name (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "pool=<pool>"
Pool name (name; values from .pools)
.TP
.B "volume=<volume>[,...]"
Volume name (name; values from .media; several values separated by commas)
.TP
.B "drive=<drive>"
Drive number (number)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.TP
.B "catalog=<catalog>"
Catalog name (name; values from .catalogs)
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.TP
.B "truncate volstatus=Purged storage=File pool=Full yes"
truncate all purged volumes of pool Full on File
.TP
.B "truncate volstatus=Purged volume=Full\-0003"
truncate one purged volume after confirmation
.PP
\fBOrigin\fR
Bareos console command.
.SS "reload"
Reload conf file
.PP
\fBSynopsis\fR
.nf
reload
.fi
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Re\-reads the configuration; a configuration with errors is refused and the running one stays.
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.TP
.B "reload"
apply edited configuration files without restarting odir
.PP
\fBOrigin\fR
Bareos console command.
