the tables of the public schema in alphabetical order
.TP
.B "\&.sqltables catalog=MyCatalog"
the tables of the catalog MyCatalog
.PP
\fBOrigin\fR
Onesimus extension. The Bareos Director does not know this command and answers "is an invalid command".
.SS "\&.sqlschema"
Show catalog schema
.PP
\fBSynopsis\fR
.nf
\&.sqlschema [table=<table>] [catalog=<catalog>]
.fi
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Shows every column of the tables in the public schema of the catalog database with its data type, ordered by table and column position; table= restricts the output to one table. An unknown table yields an empty list, a name that is not a plain identifier is rejected. The command only reads and helps writing queries for .sql.
.PP
Onesimus extension: Bareos does not know the command and answers ".sqlschema: is an invalid command.". Besides .sqlschema in its Command ACL the console needs .sql or sqlquery, as for any raw catalog access.
.PP
\fBArguments\fR
.PP
\fI\&.sqlschema\fR
.TP
.B "table=<table>"
Table name (text)
.TP
.B "catalog=<catalog>"
Catalog name (name; values from .catalogs)
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.TP
.B "\&.sqlschema table=pool"
columns and data types of the pool table
.TP
.B "\&.sqlschema"
the columns of every catalog table
.PP
\fBOrigin\fR
Onesimus extension. The Bareos Director does not know this command and answers "is an invalid command".
.SS "\&.sqlcount"
Count catalog records
.PP
\fBSynopsis\fR
.nf
\&.sqlcount [table=<table>] [catalog=<catalog>]
.fi
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Counts the rows of catalog tables. Without an argument it reports the most important tables (client, fileset, job, jobmedia, media, pool, storage); File and Path are left out on purpose because counting them takes long in large catalogs. With table= exactly one table is counted. The command only reads.
.PP
Onesimus extension: Bareos does not know the command and answers ".sqlcount: is an invalid command.", so programs that must work with both directors should not rely on it. The console needs .sql or sqlquery in its Command ACL in addition to .sqlcount.
.PP
\fBArguments\fR
.PP
\fI\&.sqlcount\fR
.TP
.B "table=<table>"
Table name (text)
.TP
.B "catalog=<catalog>"
Catalog name (name; values from .catalogs)
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.TP
.B "\&.sqlcount"
row counts of the main catalog tables
.TP
.B "\&.sqlcount table=file"
number of rows in the file table
.PP
\fBOrigin\fR
Onesimus extension. The Bareos Director does not know this command and answers "is an invalid command".
.SS "\&.acl"
Manage console ACLs (Onesimus)
.PP
\fBSynopsis\fR
.nf
\&.acl
\&.acl list [console=<console>]
\&.acl set console=<console> [jobacl=<jobacl>[,...] ...] [clientacl=<clientacl>[,...] ...] [storageacl=<storageacl>[,...] ...] [scheduleacl=<scheduleacl>[,...] ...] [poolacl=<poolacl>[,...] ...] [commandacl=<commandacl>[,...] ...] [filesetacl=<filesetacl>[,...] ...] [catalogacl=<catalogacl>[,...] ...] [whereacl=<whereacl>[,...] ...] [pluginoptionsacl=<pluginoptionsacl>[,...] ...]
\&.acl delete console=<console> [jobacl[=<jobacl>[,...]] ...] [clientacl[=<clientacl>[,...]] ...] [storageacl[=<storageacl>[,...]] ...] [scheduleacl[=<scheduleacl>[,...]] ...] [poolacl[=<poolacl>[,...]] ...] [commandacl[=<commandacl>[,...]] ...] [filesetacl[=<filesetacl>[,...]] ...] [catalogacl[=<catalogacl>[,...]] ...] [whereacl[=<whereacl>[,...]] ...] [pluginoptionsacl[=<pluginoptionsacl>[,...]] ...]
\&.acl clear console=<console>
\&.acl copy from=<from> to=<to>
.fi
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Shows and changes the catalog tier of the two\-tier console ACLs. The ACL directives of the Console and Profile resources are the outer frame (changed in the editor); the catalog ACL can only restrict further. Effective is what both allow.
.PP
set, delete, clear and copy need the CommandACL .acl and configure. Entries are comma separated; commas inside {}, [] or () belong to the entry (regular expressions), a repeated key adds entries.
.PP
\fBSubcommands\fR
.TP
.B "\&.acl list"
File and catalog entries, effective result
.IP
Shows per ACL type the file entries (first those of the console, then those of its profiles), the catalog entries and the effective result, plus the load state of the catalog ACL. list is also the default when no subcommand is given. Without console= the own console is shown, or all consoles for a console that may use configure; the ACLs of another console need configure. Catalog entries that only allow what the file ACL forbids are marked as having no effect.
.TP
.B "\&.acl set"
Replace catalog entries of types
.IP
Replaces the catalog list of the console for every ACL type given. Entries are evaluated like a Bareos list: the first matching entry decides, ! forbids, regular expressions and *all* work as in the file, and a name no entry matches is forbidden. The change takes effect at once. Needs the CommandACL .acl and configure.
.IP
The catalog ACL of another console may be changed freely, since it can never go beyond that console's file ACL. On the own console only a narrowing change is allowed: a first list for a type without catalog entries, or a list made from the old one only by inserting ! entries and removing entries without !.
.TP
.B "\&.acl delete"
Delete catalog entries
.IP
Removes the given entries from the catalog ACL of the console; a type key without a value removes the whole catalog list of that type, which then no longer restricts. An entry the catalog ACL does not have is an error and nothing changes. Works also for a console that is no longer configured but still has catalog entries. Needs the CommandACL .acl and configure; on the own console only removing entries without ! is allowed.
.TP
.B "\&.acl clear"
Delete every catalog entry of a console
.IP
Removes all catalog ACL entries of the console, so only its file ACL applies again. Works also for a console that is no longer configured. Needs the CommandACL .acl and configure and is refused on the own console, since it could widen the rights.
.TP
.B "\&.acl copy"
Copy the catalog entries of a console
.IP
Gives the console to= the catalog ACL lists of the console from=. Types that from= has no catalog entries for lose their entries at to=. The file ACLs of both consoles stay as they are. Needs the CommandACL .acl and configure.
.PP
\fBArguments\fR
.PP
\fI\&.acl list\fR
.TP
.B "console=<console>"
Console name (name; values from .consoles)
.PP
\fI\&.acl set\fR
.TP
.B "console=<console>"
Console name (name; values from .consoles; required)
.TP
.B "jobacl=<jobacl>[,...] ..."
Catalog ACL entries (comma list, repeatable) (text; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "clientacl=<clientacl>[,...] ..."
Catalog ACL entries (comma list, repeatable) (text; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "storageacl=<storageacl>[,...] ..."
Catalog ACL entries (comma list, repeatable) (text; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "scheduleacl=<scheduleacl>[,...] ..."
Catalog ACL entries (comma list, repeatable) (text; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "poolacl=<poolacl>[,...] ..."
Catalog ACL entries (comma list, repeatable) (text; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "commandacl=<commandacl>[,...] ..."
Catalog ACL entries (comma list, repeatable) (text; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "filesetacl=<filesetacl>[,...] ..."
Catalog ACL entries (comma list, repeatable) (text; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "catalogacl=<catalogacl>[,...] ..."
Catalog ACL entries (comma list, repeatable) (text; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "whereacl=<whereacl>[,...] ..."
Catalog ACL entries (comma list, repeatable) (text; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "pluginoptionsacl=<pluginoptionsacl>[,...] ..."
Catalog ACL entries (comma list, repeatable) (text; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.PP
\fI\&.acl delete\fR
.TP
.B "console=<console>"
Console name (name; values from .consoles; required)
.TP
.B "jobacl[=<jobacl>[,...]] ..."
Entries to delete; without value every entry of the type (text; the value may be left out; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "clientacl[=<clientacl>[,...]] ..."
Entries to delete; without value every entry of the type (text; the value may be left out; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "storageacl[=<storageacl>[,...]] ..."
Entries to delete; without value every entry of the type (text; the value may be left out; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "scheduleacl[=<scheduleacl>[,...]] ..."
Entries to delete; without value every entry of the type (text; the value may be left out; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "poolacl[=<poolacl>[,...]] ..."
Entries to delete; without value every entry of the type (text; the value may be left out; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "commandacl[=<commandacl>[,...]] ..."
Entries to delete; without value every entry of the type (text; the value may be left out; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "filesetacl[=<filesetacl>[,...]] ..."
Entries to delete; without value every entry of the type (text; the value may be left out; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "catalogacl[=<catalogacl>[,...]] ..."
Entries to delete; without value every entry of the type (text; the value may be left out; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "whereacl[=<whereacl>[,...]] ..."
Entries to delete; without value every entry of the type (text; the value may be left out; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.TP
.B "pluginoptionsacl[=<pluginoptionsacl>[,...]] ..."
Entries to delete; without value every entry of the type (text; the value may be left out; several values separated by commas; may be repeated)
.PP
\fI\&.acl clear\fR
.TP
.B "console=<console>"
Console name (name; values from .consoles; required)
